  "narrative": "The new batch provides strong internal robustness evidence for the three large associations and mostly null context dependence. In TP53- and SMARCA4-wildtype cells, KEAP1 loss has a signed effect of +0.784 (R14: +0.736 to +0.833); in KEAP1- and SMARCA4-wildtype cells, TP53 loss has a signed effect of +0.804 (R15: +0.757 to +0.850); and in TP53- and KEAP1-wildtype cells, SMARCA4 loss has a signed effect of +0.814 (R16: +0.768 to +0.860). All are far above the 0.15-unit threshold, so I accept H28, H29, and H30. These are overlapping analyses of the same supplied dataset, not independent replication, but they make it less likely that each association is produced only by co-occurrence with the other two losses. The non-Avana library strata are smaller but valid: KEAP1 loss signed +0.881 (R20: +0.694 to +1.068) and SMARCA4 loss signed +0.909 (R21: +0.783 to +1.035). I accept H26 and H27 as threshold-level dataset associations, keeping them active because the non-Avana cell counts are modest and because technical stratification remains an important robustness check rather than a causal claim. The interaction evidence is much weaker. TP53-loss effect modification by KEAP1 loss is +0.077 (R17: -0.042 to +0.196); the point estimate is below threshold and the interval is imprecise, so H25 is unresolved but deferred rather than a priority. The other two interactions are inconsistent with threshold-level context dependence: SMARCA4-loss effect modification by TP53 loss is signed negative at -0.070 (R18: -0.192 to +0.053), and KEAP1-loss effect modification by SMARCA4 loss is signed negative at -0.018 (R19: -0.161 to +0.124); their upper bounds are below the claimed threshold, so H31 and H33 are rejected and closed. KRAS and ARID1A screens are null or opposite and do not support threshold-level associations (R24 and R25 upper bounds +0.049 and +0.017 respectively), so H36 and H37 are rejected and closed. CDKN2A remains borderline: in TP53/MTAP-wildtype cells the signed effect is +0.142 (R22: +0.059 to +0.224), and the adenocarcinoma interaction is +0.050 (R23: -0.120 to +0.221). Both point estimates are below the 0.15-unit threshold despite intervals that include larger values, so H34 and H35 remain unresolved and deferred; there is not yet evidence for a scientifically threshold-level CDKN2A association. I request independent validation for H13, the main TP53-loss association with weaker composite dependency, because it was accepted after a post-hoc reversal of the original direction and has not received validation; H29 provides internal robustness but not independent evidence. All accepted findings remain observational associations within this supplied dataset.",
