  "research_notes": "Round 2 discovery appraisal: Three accepted main associations are now reinforced by internal robustness analyses. KEAP1 loss (weaker composite dependency) remains strong in TP53/SMARCA4-wildtype cells (R14 +0.784, +0.736 to +0.833) and non-Avana library cells (R20 +0.881, +0.694 to +1.068); H3 was already independently validated (R13 +0.738, +0.644 to +0.831). TP53 loss (weaker dependency) remains strong in KEAP1/SMARCA4-wildtype cells (R15 +0.804, +0.757 to +0.850), but the main claim H13 is still unvalidated and was a post-discovery direction reversal; independent validation requested for H13. SMARCA4 loss (stronger dependency) remains strong in TP53/KEAP1-wildtype cells (R16 +0.814, +0.768 to +0.860) and non-Avana library cells (R21 +0.909, +0.783 to +1.035). Pairwise interactions among TP53, KEAP1, and SMARCA4 are not strong: H25 is deferred unresolved; H31 and H33 are rejected/closed. Broad screens for KRAS and ARID1A are rejected/closed. CDKN2A remains borderline below threshold in full population (R6 +0.139) and TP53/MTAP-wildtype context (R22 +0.142); subtype interaction is small (R23 +0.050); H6, H34, and H35 are unresolved/deferred. Next priorities after validation: use unrun registered comparisons H14, H15, H17-H24, H32, and H38 to assess remaining stratifications (STK11, single-gene wildtype, Avana-library main effects, lineage interactions) and consider new technical checks such as screen batch or culture type if registered. Maintain distinction: accepted claims are dataset associations, not causal mechanisms or generalizable findings.",
